## Plan

_Written by `claude-6` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/40815027227)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

A press on the playmat should tap everywhere except on a card or a board control. A tap is a mark plus a sound, in the family of the half it lands in (#1954, #2015). That includes the margin of a zone holding a unit or a set trap, which is the `zone-…` div itself. `isEmptySurfaceTarget` in `apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.tsx` loses its occupied-zone check and keeps only its existing `closest` list. These still stop a tap: the card sprite, a legal zone (`role="button"`), `disabled` and `data-dragging`. Two comments say a slot with a card belongs to that card, and both are rewritten. Three new tests in `SandSurface.test.tsx` cover the acceptance items.

## Files to touch

| Path | Kind | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.tsx` | change | The header comment (lines 1–5). In `isEmptySurfaceTarget`, remove the `zone` lookup and its comment and return the `closest` test. |
| `apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.test.tsx` | change | One header line, two imports, a `boardField` helper and three `#2332` tests in `describe("SandSurface taps")`. |

Touch nothing else:
- no other file in `apps/web` (`Zone.tsx`, `Board.tsx`, `Board.test.tsx` and `board.css` stay as they are);
- nothing in `crates/`, `spec/` or `e2e/`;
- no catalog change, no patches fragment, no ruling.

No spec section or ruling governs this, because the layer is cosmetic. CLAUDE.md rule 7 still holds: the layer reads no rules and no hidden state.

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.tsx`, header (lines 1–5).** Replace the five comment lines with exactly this:

   ```ts
   // A cosmetic, input-transparent fidget layer for the playmat. It reads neither rules nor hidden
   // state: the board owns the cards above it, and this layer only records pointer marks where a
   // press landed on neither a card nor a board control. #2332: a zone's own margin, around the unit
   // or trap it holds, is playmat too. #1954: one press is one tap, in the look and sound of the
   // playmat's family; holding or dragging adds nothing. #2015: a tap takes the playmat of the half
   // it lands on, the opponent's above the centre line.
   ```

2. **Same file, `function isEmptySurfaceTarget`.** Keep its name and signature. Replace its body with exactly this:

   ```ts
     if (!(target instanceof Element)) return false;
     // #2332: every bit of the playmat taps, an occupied zone's margin included. Only a card, a board
     // control or a legal zone (a button: the press plays into it) keeps the press.
     return target.closest(".card, button, input, select, textarea, [role=button], .hero, .seat, .control-bar") === null;
   ```

   Three lines go away: `const zone = …`, its `// A blank lane slot …` comment and `return zone === null || …`. Change nothing else in the file; the `down` handler's `disabledRef` and `data-dragging` checks stay.

3. **`apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.test.tsx`, imports.**
   - Change `import { fullBoardView } from "../test/fixtures.ts";` to `import { baseView, fullBoardView } from "../test/fixtures.ts";`.
   - Add `import { testid } from "./contract.ts";` directly after the line `import Board from "./Board.tsx";`.

4. **Same file, header (lines 1–3).** Add this line after line 3:
   `// #2332: an occupied zone's own element taps too; only its card and the board's controls keep a press.`

5. **Same file, a helper.** Put it after `function playedIds()` and before `describe`:

   ```tsx
   /** #2332: `fullBoardView`, every zone holding a card, on the marble playmat; returns its stubbed field. */
   function boardField(): HTMLElement {
     const mounted = render(
       <Board view={fullBoardView()} wearCosmetics deckCosmetics={{ table: "table-marble", field: null, cardBack: null }} />,
     );
     const field = mounted.container.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".field");
     if (field === null) throw new Error("fixture must draw a field");
     stubBounds(field);
     return field;
   }
   ```

6. **Same file, three tests.** Add them at the end of `describe("SandSurface taps")`, after the `#1954 neon's hue …` test. Their bodies are under **Tests**.

## Tests

All three go in `apps/web/src/game/SandSurface.test.tsx`, inside `describe("SandSurface taps")`.

- `it("#2332 a press on an occupied zone's own element, beside its card, taps in that half's playmat", () => { … })`:

  ```tsx
  const field = boardField();
  const zone = screen.getByTestId(testid.zone("you", "units", 1));
  expect(zone.querySelector(".card")).not.toBeNull();

  press(zone);
  expect(field.querySelector(".tap-mark--stone")).not.toBeNull();
  expect(playedIds()).toEqual([TAP_SFX[TAP_FAMILY["table-marble"]]]);
  ```

  This test fails on the unchanged source, because the old check drops the press: no mark and no `playSfx` call. `press` uses its default y = 70, which is the viewer's half, so the tap takes the marble playmat's stone family.

- `it("#2332 a press inside an occupied zone's card does not tap", () => { … })`:

  ```tsx
  const field = boardField();
  const zone = screen.getByTestId(testid.zone("you", "units", 1));
  const sprite = zone.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".card *");
  if (sprite === null) throw new Error("a unit's card must draw its face");

  press(sprite);
  expect(markCount(field)).toBe(0);
  expect(audio.playSfx).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  ```

- `it("#2332 a press on a legal zone does not tap: the press plays into it", () => { … })`:

  ```tsx
  const legal = testid.zone("you", "units", 1);
  const mounted = render(<Board view={baseView()} highlight={{ legal: new Set([legal]), selected: new Set() }} />);
  const field = mounted.container.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".field");
  if (field === null) throw new Error("fixture must draw a field");
  stubBounds(field);
  const zone = screen.getByTestId(legal);
  expect(zone.getAttribute("role")).toBe("button");

  press(zone);
  expect(markCount(field)).toBe(0);
  expect(audio.playSfx).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  ```

  This test uses `baseView()` because its boards are empty, so `Zone.tsx` makes the legal zone a button. `fullBoardView()` has no empty zone.

These existing tests must stay green without changes: the `#1954` and `#2015` tests in this file, and the `Board.test.tsx` test "leaves every pointer gesture with a card or active interaction alone, while empty sand marks immediately".

I ran the two files at the base commit, after building the wasm engine: 37 of 37 tests pass. Commands to run:

```
sh scripts/build-wasm.sh
pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/game/SandSurface.test.tsx src/game/Board.test.tsx
pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck
pnpm exec eslint apps/web e2e
pnpm --dir apps/web test
```

The first command builds the wasm engine the tests import; it only needs to run once.

## Done when

- [ ] `isEmptySurfaceTarget` returns only the `closest` test, with no `zone` or `.card` lookup left.
- [ ] Neither the header of `SandSurface.tsx` nor the comment in `isEmptySurfaceTarget` says a slot with a card belongs to that card.
- [ ] The three `#2332` tests pass, and the first one fails on the unchanged source.
- [ ] Every existing test in `SandSurface.test.tsx` and `Board.test.tsx` passes unchanged.
- [ ] The web's typecheck, eslint and full unit tests pass.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass: rustfmt, catalog, patches, rulings, clippy, cargo tests and web tests.

## Risks

- **An occupied legal zone.** After the change, a press on any zone's padding taps, and if the zone is legal the press also reaches `Zone`'s `onClick`.
  - An empty legal zone is `role="button"`, so it stays excluded.
  - An occupied legal zone is `role="group"`, so a press on its margin now both taps and plays.
  - While a card is lifted or targeted, `sandDisabled` turns the surface off anyway (`Game.tsx`: `interaction.stage !== "idle"`). So this only shows up when a prompt offers an occupied zone.
  - The issue sets the exclusion list, so do not add `[data-legal]` to it (see Open questions).
- **Determinism, replay, hidden information:** not affected, since the surface is cosmetic and reads no view state.
- **Test fragility:** `screen.getByTestId(testid.zone(...))` needs exactly one matching zone in the document. Each test renders one `Board`, and `afterEach` runs `cleanup()`, so this holds.

## Open questions

- After this change, an occupied zone the player may pick (`data-legal="true"`, `role="group"`) taps when its margin is pressed; the role is `group` because its card takes focus. The issue keeps the existing `closest` list, so the plan follows it. A person may want `[data-legal='true']` added to that list in a follow-up.
